# the repo is LF; git checks out CRLF on windows where it matters. without
# this, files committed from windows and files committed from CI disagree and
# every diff is the whole file.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webm binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary

# bundled mod payloads have their sha256 pinned in the manifests, so git must
# hand every platform the same bytes. a readme that used to ship beside the
# XIII-2 audio fix was plain text, which "* text=auto" happily
# normalised: it was pinned from a CRLF working tree and checks out LF, so the
# hash missed and the patch reported "not the build this patcher ships" on
# every machine that cloned after eol=lf landed. a pinned file cannot be a file
# git is allowed to rewrite.
assets/mods/** -text

# same reasoning, different files. tests/data holds samples of other people's
# formats: a real filelist index, and the HD Project's CRLF recipe files. A
# fixture that git normalises stops being a sample of the thing it is there to
# prove we can read, and the CRLF warning on checking these in was the audio
# fix bug announcing itself a second time.
tests/data/** -text

